  {
   "id": "GcNssOPsAgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2015-09-16T12:47:58Z",
   "subject": "Re: Interaction effects in latent growth curve models",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>what does it mean that &quot;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;color:rgb(106,106,106);font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:18px\">Interaction terms</span><span style=\"color:rgb(84,84,84);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;line-height:18px\"> are currently not supported&quot; in the </span><span style=\"color:rgb(68,68,68);font-family:HelveticaNeue,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px\">special </span><code style=\"padding-right:2px;padding-left:2px;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:14px;line-height:21px;vertical-align:baseline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;color:rgb(68,68,68)\">growth()</code><span style=\"color:rgb(68,68,68);font-family:HelveticaNeue,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:21px\"> function of lavaan?</span><span style=\"color:rgb(84,84,84);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;line-height:18px\"> </span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div>It means you can&#39;t use the asterisk operator to automatically calculate product terms, like you can in lm() and glm().  And there is no support for latent moderated structural equations (but the semTools package has functions to support latent interactions using product indicators).</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(84,84,84);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;line-height:18px\">Would the estimates be wrong if I compute an interaction term (i.e., </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0);font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;line-height:24px;font-size:12px;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">StPov</span><span style=\"color:rgb(84,84,84);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;line-height:18px\">)  manually in order to regress it on i &amp; s? </span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div>Yes, if State and Poverty are observed variables in your model, you need to add the product term StPov to your data.frame in order to include it in your model.</div><div><br></div><div>Terry</div><div><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
