>Would the estimates be wrong if I compute an interaction term (i.e., </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0);font-family:Consolas,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;line-height:24px;font-size:12px;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">StPov</span><span style=\"color:rgb(84,84,84);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;line-height:18px\">)  manually in order to regress it on i &amp; s? </span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Yes, if State and Poverty are observed variables in your model, you need to add the product term StPov to your data.frame in order to include it in your model.</div><div><br></div><div>Terry</div><div><br></div></blockquote></div></div>"
